[Description]
{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Fennario;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\hyphpar0\sl288\slmult1\cf1\f0\fs18 You joined the revolt in 1400. Grabbed a bunch of your boys, found some weapons, and prepared to kill some of the bishop's men. Didn't go well. Most of your friends were killed by knights. Big Cuno spit in Herr Gebelstadt's face and was drawn and quartered on the spot. You fled into the woods. Barely survived. But when you got back to Wurzberg, you were arrested for treason. But the old bishop Gerhard said he saw God's Grace in your eyes and forgave you. Gave you a good job at the church, digging the graves and helping clean up the rectory. You don't know why you deserved that. Maybe the bishop confused you with someone else? Best not to ask some questions.\par \pard\cf0\f1\fs20 \par }

